   "html_text": "The rules for synthetic demonstrations lead to a list of criticisms of “geometers”. Chapter 4 notes some equivocations in Euclid’s use of “angle”, “ratio”, and “proportion.” Later mathematicians are criticizes for not respecting the distinction between nominal and real definitions. The former should be stipulations about how words are associated with ideas. The latter should characterize the nature of the object being defined. Examples are given about disputes among prominent mathematicians over",
